ugin/cli/"},{"url":"https://v2.tauri.app/ko/security/capabilities/"},{"url":"https://v2.tauri.app/ko/plugin/cli/"},{"url":"https://v2.tauri.app/ko/learn/security/using-plugin-permissions/"}]},{"domain":"dockview.dev","entries":[{"url":"https://dockview.dev/docs/overview/whats-new-v7/"}]},{"domain":"xtermjs.org","entries":[{"url":"https://xtermjs.org/docs/guides/flowcontrol/"}]}]},"recipient":"all","channel":"analysis"},{"id":"ba75bfe1-e80b-41ad-98e0-9e21a3c6480d","author":{"role":"assistant","name":null,"metadata":{}},"create_time":1786701545.592087,"update_time":null,"content":{"content_type":"thoughts","thoughts":[{"summary":"Planning the Chinese research report","content":"I’m preparing a report-only answer in Chinese, using four to eight major sections and citations for researched claims. I’m treating the three named projects as working assumptions because their internal documentation isn’t available, and I’m not relying on the earlier architecture description.\n\nA key finding is that Tauri’s platform webviews differ, so Electron may offer a more straightforward cross-platform CDP path. I’ll compare architecture options, risks, milestones, interfaces, and implementation patterns.","chunks":[],"finished":true},{"summary":"Designing the integrated research report","content":"I’m treating the three projects as proposed profiles rather than asserting undocumented architecture. The report will compare desktop-shell, browser, terminal, state, security, plugin, and evidence-loop options, then recommend a shared workbench core.\n\nThe central engineering caution is that native browser surfaces don’t behave like ordinary React tiles. I’m therefore favoring constrained browser-stage placement for the first release, with previews elsewhere, instead of promising unrestricted docking everywhere.","chunks":[],"finished":true},{"summary":"Planned and designed the integrated Chinese research report","content":"","chunks":[],"finished":true}],"source_analysis_msg_id":"47f3e8ad-