de/features/web-dashboard-Web Dashboard | Hermes Agent - nous research","title":"Web Dashboard | Hermes Agent - nous research","items":[{"url":"https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/docs/user-guide/features/web-dashboard","domain":"hermes-agent.nousresearch.com","title":"Web Dashboard | Hermes Agent - nous research","snippet":"The web dashboard is a browser-based UI for managing your Hermes Agent installation. you can configure settings, manage API keys, and monitor sessions from a ..."}]}]},{"key":"https://nesquena.github.io/hermes-webui/","domain":"nesquena.github.io","url":"https://nesquena.github.io/hermes-webui/","titles":[{"key":"https://nesquena.github.io/hermes-webui/-Hermes — Community Web UI","title":"Hermes — Community Web UI","items":[{"url":"https://nesquena.github.io/hermes-webui/","domain":"nesquena.github.io","title":"Hermes — Community Web UI","snippet":"Hermes Agent. The self-improving AI agent that runs on your server. Layered memory that accumulates across sessions, a cron scheduler that fires ..."}]}]},{"key":"https://skillsllm.com/skill/hermes-webui","domain":"skillsllm.com","url":"https://skillsllm.com/skill/hermes-webui","titles":[{"key":"https://skillsllm.com/skill/hermes-webui-hermes-webui - AI Agents on GitHub","title":"hermes-webui - AI Agents on GitHub","items":[{"url":"https://skillsllm.com/skill/hermes-webui","domain":"skillsllm.com","title":"hermes-webui - AI Agents on GitHub","snippet":"28 May 2026 — hermes-webui is an open-source ai agents skill for AI coding assistants such as Claude Code, Codex CLI, and ChatGPT, built by sanchomuzax."}]}]},{"key":"https://hermes-workspace.com/","domain":"hermes-workspace.com","url":"https://hermes-workspace.com/","titles":[{"key":"https://hermes-workspace.com/-Hermes Workspace · Your AI agent's command center","title":"Hermes Workspace · Your AI agent's command center","items":[{"url":"https://hermes-workspace.com/","domain":"hermes-workspace.com","title":"Hermes Workspace · Your AI agent's command center","snippet":"Open-source web UI for your agent. Chat, memory, skills, terminal, and files in one interface."}]}]},{"key":"https://gitverse.ru/yatul/hermes-webui","domain":"gitverse.ru","url":"https://gitverse.ru/yatul/hermes-webui","titles":[{"key":"https://gitverse.ru/yatul/hermes-webui-yatul/hermes-webui","title":"yatul/hermes-webui","items":[{"url":"https://gitverse.ru/yatul/hermes-webui","domain":"gitverse.ru","title":"yatul/hermes-webui","snippet":"2 days ago — Hermes WebUI is a lightweight, dark-themed web app interface in your browser for Hermes Agent. Full parity with the CLI experience ..."}]}]},{"key":"https://thenewstack.io/github-copilot-desktop-app/","domain":"thenewstack.io","url":"https://thenewstack.io/github-copilot-desktop-app/","titles":[{"key":"https://thenewstack.io/github-copilot-desktop-app/-GitHub takes aim at Claude Code and Codex with its ...","title":"GitHub takes aim at Claude Code and Codex with its ...","items":[{"url":"https://thenewstack.io/github-copilot-desktop-app/","domain":"thenewstack.io","title":"GitHub takes aim at Claude Code and Codex with its ...","snippet":"16 May 2026 — “A standalone desktop application designed to manage coding agents, issues, pull requests and development sessions from a single interface.” The ...Read more"}]}]},{"key":"https://www.theverge.com/tech/930447/microsoft-claude-code-discontinued-notepad","domain":"theverge.com","url":"https://www.theverge.com/tech/930447/microsoft-claude-code-discontinued-notepad","titles":[{"key":"https://www.theverge.com/tech/930447/microsoft-claude-code-discontinued-notepad-Microsoft starts canceling Claude Code licenses","title":"Microsoft starts canceling Claude Code licenses","items":[{"url":"https://www.theverge.com/tech/930447/microsoft-claude-code-discontinued-notepad","domain":"theverge.com","title":"Microsoft starts canceling Claude Code licenses","snippet":"Microsoft is discontinuing most licenses for Claude Code, Anthropic's AI coding tool, which had become very popular internally since its rollout in December. The company is shifting developers toward GitHub Copilot CLI, its in-house command line coding assistant, citing the need to align workflows across teams like Windows, Outlook, and Microsoft 365. The transition comes with a June 30 deadline, coinciding with the end of Microsoft’s fiscal year, suggesting cost-cutting is also a motivation behind the move.\n\nWhile Claude Code helped non-developers such as designers and project managers engage with coding for the first time, Microsoft now wants to standardize on Copilot CLI, which it can further customize to meet its internal needs. Claude models will still be available through Copilot CLI, and the Foundry partnership with Anthropic, including models like Claude Opus and Sonnet, remains unaffected.\n\nDespite Claude Code's popularity, Microsoft emphasizes its collaboration with GitHub to enhance Copilot CLI based on internal usage feedback. The company is also reportedly exploring partnerships with other AI startups to strengthen its development tools ecosystem while avoiding antitrust scrutiny.","pub_date":1778785200}]}]},{"key":"https://www.techradar.com/pro/github-integrates-claude-and-codex-ai-coding-agents-directly-into-github","domain":"techradar.com","url":"https://www.techradar.com/pro/github-integrates-claude-and-codex-ai-coding-agents-directly-into-github","titles":[{"key":"https://www.techradar.com/pro/github-integrates-claude-and-codex-ai-coding-agents-directly-into-github-GitHub integrates Claude and Codex AI coding agents directly into GitHub","title":"GitHub integrates Claude and Codex AI coding agents directly into GitHub","items":[{"url":"https://www.techradar.com/pro/github-integrates-claude-and-codex-ai-coding-agents-directly-into-github","domain":"techradar.com","title":"GitHub integrates Claude and Codex AI coding agents directly into GitHub","snippet":"GitHub has announced the integration of additional AI coding agents—Anthropic’s Claude and OpenAI’s Codex—directly into its platform, broadening its AI tool offerings beyond its in-house Copilot. These agents are now available to Copilot Pro+ and Copilot Enterprise users across GitHub’s website, mobile app, and Visual Studio Code, enabling a more flexible and seamless development experience. Users can invoke agents directly through issues, pull requests, the Agents tab, or the agent sessions view. During the public preview phase, each agent session consumes one premium request, with formal pricing yet to be revealed.\n\nThis new functionality also allows multiple agents to collaboratively generate draft pull requests and supports user interactions with agents via @copilot, @claude, or @codex mentions, replicating teamwork with human developers. GitHub is also working on integrating more agents from other companies such as Google, Cognition, and xAI, reinforcing its commitment to expanding developer access to diverse AI tools within their core workflows.","pub_date":1770293700}]}]},{"key":"https://www.windowscentral.com/microsoft/microsoft-cancels-claude-code-licenses-shifting-developers-to-github-copilot-cli-a-move-likely-driven-by-financial-motives","domain":"windowscentral.com","url":"https://www.windowscentral.com/microsoft/microsoft-cancels-claude-code-licenses-shifting-developers-to-github-copilot-cli-a-move-likely-driven-by-financial-motives","titles":[{"key":"https://www.windowscentral.com/microsoft/microsoft-cancels-claude-code-licenses-shifting-developers-to-github-copilot-cli-a-move-likely-driven-by-financial-motives-Microsoft cancels Claude Code licenses, shifting developers to GitHub Copilot CLI - a move likely driven by financial motives","title":"Microsoft cancels Claude Code licenses, shifting developers to GitHub Copilot CLI - a move likely driven by financial motives","items":[{"url":"https://www.windowscentral.com/microsoft/microsoft-cancels-claude-code-licenses-shifting-developers-to-github-copilot-cli-a-move-likely-driven-by-financial-motives","domain":"windowscentral.com","title":"Microsoft cancels Claude Code licenses, shifting developers to GitHub Copilot CLI - a move likely driven by financial motives","snippet":"Microsoft is phasing out its use of Anthropic’s Claude Code among employees and transitioning to its proprietary GitHub Copilot CLI tool. This shift, set to be completed by the end of June 2026, primarily affects the Experiences + Devices division—covering Windows, Microsoft 365, Outlook, Teams, and Surface. Claude Code had gained substantial popularity within Microsoft since its introduction in December of the previous year, praised for its useful features and effectiveness in real engineering workflows. However, Copilot CLI allows Microsoft more direct control over integration, workflows, and security, and aligns better with GitHub's ecosystem, which Microsoft owns.\n\nThe move is not based solely on technology but is also influenced by financial considerations, particularly with Microsoft’s fiscal year ending June 30. Canceling Claude Code licenses could help reduce operational costs. Although employee feedback favored Claude Code, the dual-tool experiment was intended to assess which AI tool better supported the company’s engineering needs. Microsoft is also exploring other AI acquisitions, such as Cursor AI, though regulatory hurdles may arise due to its similarity to GitHub Copilot.","pub_date":1778851998}]}]},{"key":"https://www.windowscentral.com/artificial-intelligence/anthropics-claude-code-is-now-available-on-the-web-for-its-pro-and-max-users","domain":"windowscentral.com","url":"https://www.windowscentral.com/artificial-intelligence/anthropics-claude-code-is-now-available-on-the-web-for-its-pro-and-max-users","titles":[{"key":"https://www.windowscentral.com/artificial-intelligence/anthropics-claude-code-is-now-available-on-the-web-for-its-pro-and-max-users-Claude Code comes to the web - so you can pay to manage the AI that's taking your job","title":"Claude Code comes to the web - so you can pay to manage the AI that's taking your job","items":[{"url":"https://www.windowscentral.com/artificial-intelligence/anthropics-claude-code-is-now-available-on-the-web-for-its-pro-and-max-users","domain":"windowscentral.com","title":"Claude Code comes to the web - so you can pay to manage the AI that's taking your job","snippet":"Anthropic has launched a web-based version of its AI coding assistant, Claude Code, expanding its accessibility beyond IDEs like Visual Studio. Now available to Pro and Max subscribers in a research preview phase, the tool allows developers to run coding tasks directly from their browser by linking Claude to their GitHub repositories. Once connected, Claude clones the repo to a secure Anthropic-managed virtual machine, sets up the environment, and can analyze, edit, test, and push changes, even creating pull requests automatically.\n\nThe virtual machine supports multiple programming languages including Python, Node.js, Java, Rust, and C++, and employs strong security measures such as isolated sessions and restricted network access. Users can also switch between local setups and the web tool easily. Though currently limited to GitHub and subject to usage rate caps, Claude Code marks a significant move toward accessible, cloud-based AI development.\n\nThis release aligns with Anthropic's broader strategy, including its partnership with Microsoft to bring Claude to Azure and integrate it into Microsoft 365 tools. It underscores Anthropic’s push toward a secure, powerful AI ecosystem aimed at both enterprise and individual developers.","pub_date":1761304102}]}]},{"key":"https://www.itpro.com/software/development/anthropic-claude-code-for-web-closed-beta-launch","domain":"itpro.com","url":"https://www.itpro.com/software/development/anthropic-claude-code-for-web-closed-beta-launch","titles":[{"key":"https://www.itpro.com/software/development/anthropic-claude-code-for-web-closed-beta-launch-Anthropic's new Claude Code web portal aims to make AI coding even more accessible","title":"Anthropic's new Claude Code web portal aims to make AI coding even more accessible","items":[{"url":"https://www.itpro.com/software/development/anthropic-claude-code-for-web-closed-beta-launch","domain":"itpro.com","title":"Anthropic's new Claude Code web portal aims to make AI coding even more accessible","snippet":"Anthropic has launched a new browser-based interface for its AI coding assistant, Claude Code, available as a closed beta for Pro and Max users. The new portal runs within users' preferred web browsers or a dedicated iOS app, eliminating the need for a command-line interface and offering integration with GitHub repositories. It is designed to streamline development workflows by aiding in tasks like bug fixes, quality assurance, and test-driven development through an intuitive interface that supports parallel task execution.\n\nSecurity is a major focus of this release. Claude Code now operates in isolated sandbox cloud environments using a secure proxy to connect with enterprise Git repositories. Admins can define strict access rules to directories and network hosts, restricting the AI's actions and mitigating risks such as prompt injection attacks and malware downloads. The service runs on Anthropic-managed infrastructure hosted on AWS. A wider release timeline has yet to be announced.","pub_date":1761119100}]}]},{"key":"https://www.tomsguide.com/ai/claude-code-just-came-to-the-web-and-its-about-to-change-how-you-vibe-code","domain":"tomsguide.com","url":"https://www.tomsguide.com/ai/claude-code-just-came-to-the-web-and-its-about-to-change-how-you-vibe-code","titles":[{"key":"https://www.tomsguide.com/ai/claude-code-just-came-to-the-web-and-its-about-to-change-how-you-vibe-code-Claude Code just came to the web - and it's about to change how you vibe code","title":"Claude Code just came to the web - and it's about to change how you vibe code","items":[{"url":"https://www.tomsguide.com/ai/claude-code-just-came-to-the-web-and-its-about-to-change-how-you-vibe-code","domain":"tomsguide.com","title":"Claude Code just came to the web - and it's about to change how you vibe code","snippet":"Anthropic has launched a web-based version of Claude Code, a major step forward in AI-assisted software development. Now in research preview for Claude Pro and Max users, the tool enables developers to write, fix, and manage code directly from the browser—no command line setup required. The platform integrates tightly with GitHub, runs entirely in the cloud, and supports features like pull request generation, secure sandbox testing, and concurrent task handling. Users can delegate multiple tasks simultaneously by simply describing what they want done, allowing Claude to function like a virtual team of developers.\n\nThe update eliminates the need to switch between tools by combining GitHub access and AI-driven automation within a single interface. Claude Code is also slated for iOS access, extending its functionality to mobile workflows. This aligns with Anthropic’s recent AI advancements, including the Claude Sonnet 4.5 and Haiku 4.5 models, and reflects the tool’s growing adoption—now reportedly generating hundreds of millions in annualized revenue. With its ability to automate and accelerate software development across experience levels, Claude Code is poised to make coding more accessible and efficient for a broad range of users.","pub_date":1760983808}]}]},{"key":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.13738","domain":"arxiv.org","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.13738","titles":[{"key":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.13738-i-Code Studio: A Configurable and Composable Framework for Integrative AI","title":"i-Code Studio: A Configurable and Composable Framework for Integrative AI","items":[{"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.13738","domain":"arxiv.org","title":"i-Code Studio: A Configurable and Composable Framework for Integrative AI","pub_date":1684824355}]}]},{"key":"https://arxiv.org/